This theory applies to highly enchanted armor and weapons
as well.  It's the rare monster that has a +3 weapon or
armor and I hardly ever find monsters with +4 or better,
yet player characters steadily ratchet up both weapons
and armor.  No matter how much +0_average stuff a monster
can start with, it isn't long before the player character
has a huge edge.  It's the nearly unlimited supply of
monsters that's used for balance, not the fact that
monsters get stronger as you go lower.  Strong and deep
characters tend to die from mistakes not from outright
combat.

