The robe brings spells to single-digit failure rates.
A level 30 wizard with a robe does not need to max out
each and every spell school to achieve 0% failure on
all time-critical spells and 9-% failure on all known
spells.  Whether you want to level up less, spend the
extra slots on polearms, spend the extra slots on random
weapons types based on artifact gifts for style reasons,
spend the extra levels on riding or hand-to-hand or
whatever, that's up to you.

When I played lawfull Valks I learned that a robe took
attack spells to low failure and cone of cold down to
0%.  That convinced me that a robe is the perfect cloak
for any spellcaster class.  Which in turn convinced me
that the [oMR is only until other sources come
available.  The result is my preference for "oR, GDSM
and so on for spell casters as well as for combat
wombats.  Robe is one of the MC=3 cloaks.  The main
reason I tend to ignore displacement is they are MC=2.

